# Live inference inputs. Every value is empty by default; there is no default key or model.
# Copy this file to .env.local (preferred) or .env. Legacy live CLIs load .env.local first;
# the designer CLI reads the exported process environment, so run `set -a; source .env.local; set +a`
# or export OPENROUTER_API_KEY and DESIGNER_MODEL before `npm run designer -- --live`.
# Never commit a real key.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# AI Puzzle Designer (v2.0). The designer protocol uses one model and no reviewer/vision roles.
# Confirmed P51 value: google/gemini-3.8-flash. The truth family uses the flat RPN wire schema.
DESIGNER_MODEL=

# Legacy v1.1 reviewer/calibration roles (historical; not used by the designer protocol).
GENERATOR_MODEL=
REVIEWER_MODEL=
ALIGNMENT_TEXT_MODEL=
VISION_REVIEWER_MODEL=

# Documented fixed limits (not secrets and not environment overrides):
# - request deadline: 90000 ms
# - response bytes: 2097152 (2 MiB)
# - input JSON text excluding base64: 65536 bytes (64 KiB)
# - PNG: 1048576 bytes (1 MiB)
# - default output cap: 8192 tokens for spec/wording/design, 4096 tokens per review
# - preflight prompt reserve: 16384 text tokens, 32768 vision tokens
# - output cap field: max_tokens when advertised, otherwise max_completion_tokens
# - routing: OpenRouter Balanced, provider fallback enabled, no provider IDs
# - designer has no reviewer/vision role separation; the legacy generator/reviewer separation remains historical

# Designer live preflight/pilot requires --routing-confirmation <path> with:
# {"operator":"<name>","checkedAt":"<ISO>","routingPolicy":"balanced","providerSort":"default","byokProviderKeysConfigured":false}
# Separate caps: --preflight-max-cost 0.50 and --max-cost 2.00 (or the explicitly authorized amounts).
# The designer model must pass the public-catalog preflight before any paid probe.

# Legacy v1.1 live preflight also requires --routing-confirmation <path> with:
# {"operator":"<name>","checkedAt":"<ISO>","providerSort":"default_balanced","byokConfigured":false}
